xnu 0439: fix the haptics boost gate and first-play order

The 0433 click voted hBoost before PLAY and set VSET from HBST 0x46, which
can read 0x80 while the rail is still starting; the first click then
reported FAULT 0x01. The donor's direct play leaves VSET clear on the first
play, writes PLAY, and raises the boost afterwards.

Make the ready gate follow the vendor wait: 0x46 bit 7 set means the boost
is on; otherwise HBST 0x0b bit 0 is busy, so ready means it is clear. Track
the boost in software for VSET, read the real HBST 0x0b in the buzz log, and
cache one SPMI channel window per APID so a click stops remapping four
windows per pattern byte (the io_submap exhaustion behind the first wedge).

